nodecode-sentinel is a rewrite of SaltProphet's SaltProphet/hermes-sentinel:
https://github.com/SaltProphet/hermes-sentinel
commit ea578eaffb871802162186adcc93ebbf71f99f92
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Justin Strange (LICENSE)

Rewritten in Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell contract: the six credential
patterns, the middle-out truncation to a character and a line bound, the loop
trap on a third identical call with its reset, and the local execution ledger
with its status/audit/reset/clear commands. The original hung these on four
Hermes hooks; here three of them ride the one `:tool` point — which the core
calls around every tool body, before and after — and the message guard is an
advice on `NLE:SUBMIT`, the one in-process ingress. Left out: the SQLite file,
because the ledger is a best-effort in-process record and a cell that writes to
disk on every call is a heavier promise than it needs to make; and the CLI
subcommand, since `/sentinel` and `(help :sentinel)` are the surfaces a
Nodecode user already has.
